# Suppress the diff for the performance dataset, without untracking it.
#
# tests/test-output/performance.json is regenerated by every `make test`, and
# because durations are recorded at nanosecond precision essentially every line
# changes each run — ~4,800 lines of noise in `git diff` for a 2.7 KB file.
#
# It CANNOT be gitignored: tests/performance_tracking.py reconstructs the
# performance history by walking this file's git log and reading each revision
# with `git show <commit>:<path>`. The file's commit history IS the dataset
# (172 commits, 2026-03 onward). Untracking it would silently empty the chart —
# the script swallows its own errors and returns [], so it would fail quietly.
#
# `-diff` marks it binary for diff purposes only. Content is stored and
# retrieved unchanged, so `git show <commit>:<path>` — the thing the tracker
# actually uses — is unaffected.
tests/test-output/performance.json -diff
